From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sdio: idle-wait in the TX thread so it is not counted as load

tx_process() polls its queues with msleep(), which sleeps in
TASK_UNINTERRUPTIBLE.  esp_TX therefore always shows as D state and adds 1
to the load average on an idle board (#15).  Sleep in TASK_IDLE for the same
number of jiffies msleep() would use (msecs_to_jiffies(n) + 1), so TX timing
is unchanged.
---
--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -1065,14 +1065,14 @@
 	while (!kthread_should_stop()) {
 
 		if (atomic_read(&context->adapter->state) < ESP_CONTEXT_READY) {
-			msleep(10);
+			schedule_timeout_idle(msecs_to_jiffies(10) + 1);
 			esp_dbg("not ready\n");
 			continue;
 		}
 
 		if (host_sleep) {
 			/* TODO: Use wait_event_interruptible_timeout */
-			msleep(100);
+			schedule_timeout_idle(msecs_to_jiffies(100) + 1);
 			continue;
 		}
 
@@ -1099,7 +1099,7 @@
 					atomic_read(&queue_items[PRIO_Q_HIGH]),
 					atomic_read(&queue_items[PRIO_Q_MID]),
 					atomic_read(&queue_items[PRIO_Q_LOW])); */
-			msleep(1);
+			schedule_timeout_idle(msecs_to_jiffies(1) + 1);
 			continue;
 		}
 
